CTF Army Knife GTFOBins integration

Includes the executable catalogue from GTFOBins (https://gtfobins.org),
curated by the GTFOBins project and its contributors.
GTFOBins is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3.
https://github.com/GTFOBins/GTFOBins.github.io

vendor/gtfobins/ is a pinned, unmodified copy of the upstream _gtfobins/
entries and the _data/functions.yml and _data/contexts.yml definitions (see
integration/gtfobins/upstream.json for the exact commit).
apps/web/lib/tools/gtfobins/data.generated.ts is derived from them by
scripts/gtfobins.mjs; entry text and code are preserved verbatim.

Community modifications: the search and browsing interface is reimplemented in
the CTF Army Knife design system, with optional placeholder substitution for
hosts, ports and file paths. These modifications do not imply any endorsement
by the original authors.

The upstream GPL-3.0 LICENSE accompanies this distribution at
vendor/gtfobins/LICENSE. Because CTF Army Knife bundles this data, the
project as a whole is distributed under GPL-3.0 (see the LICENSE file at the
repository root).
